---
import Fig from './Fig.astro';

const caption = `The affected symbol-resolution path sits behind ngu.random.bytes(); ckcc.rng_bytes() reaches the STM32 hardware TRNG directly. The dashed link is the hotfix: it rebinds the fallback generator to that same hardware.`;
---

<Fig
  id="fig-surfaces"
  viewBox="0 0 920 320"
  minWidth={680}
  title="The two RNG call surfaces"
  desc="ngu.random.bytes() reaches libngu my_random_bytes, which draws on the MicroPython Yasmarang seeded from the UID word, SysTick and RTC, and the libngu Yasmarang started from constants or an at-most-32-bit reseed. Those feed the call sites requiring review. ckcc.rng_bytes() reaches the STM32 hardware TRNG and feeds the backup password, 7z salt, HSM user secrets and SD overwrite blocks. The hotfix rebinds the first surface to the same hardware."
  caption={caption}
>
  <defs>
    <marker id="arr-sf" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
      <path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" class="ah" />
    </marker>
  </defs>

  <!-- affected surface -->
  <text class="lane bad-t" x="16" y="18">AFFECTED SURFACE</text>

  <rect class="node bad" x="16" y="40" width="180" height="50" rx="8" />
  <text class="t mono" x="106" y="70">ngu.random.bytes()</text>

  <line class="edge" x1="196" y1="65" x2="236" y2="65" marker-end="url(#arr-sf)" />

  <rect class="node bad" x="240" y="40" width="200" height="50" rx="8" />
  <text class="t mono" x="340" y="62">libngu</text>
  <text class="t mono" x="340" y="78">my_random_bytes()</text>

  <line class="edge" x1="440" y1="60" x2="496" y2="46" marker-end="url(#arr-sf)" />
  <line class="edge" x1="440" y1="72" x2="496" y2="120" marker-end="url(#arr-sf)" />

  <rect class="node bad" x="500" y="16" width="220" height="60" rx="8" />
  <text class="t" x="610" y="40">MicroPython Yasmarang</text>
  <text class="s" x="610" y="58">UID word, SysTick, RTC</text>

  <rect class="node bad" x="500" y="92" width="220" height="64" rx="8" />
  <text class="t" x="610" y="116">libngu Yasmarang</text>
  <text class="s" x="610" y="134">constants or at-most-32-bit reseed</text>

  <line class="edge" x1="720" y1="46" x2="756" y2="66" marker-end="url(#arr-sf)" />
  <line class="edge" x1="720" y1="124" x2="756" y2="106" marker-end="url(#arr-sf)" />

  <rect class="node bad" x="760" y="30" width="145" height="120" rx="8" />
  <text class="t" x="832" y="58">Call sites</text>
  <text class="t" x="832" y="74">requiring review</text>
  <text class="s" x="832" y="96">seeds, paper keys,</text>
  <text class="s" x="832" y="111">passwords, session</text>
  <text class="s" x="832" y="126">material, nonces</text>

  <!-- intact surface -->
  <text class="lane ok-t" x="16" y="188">INTACT SURFACE</text>

  <rect class="node ok" x="16" y="210" width="180" height="50" rx="8" />
  <text class="t mono" x="106" y="240">ckcc.rng_bytes()</text>

  <line class="edge" x1="196" y1="235" x2="236" y2="232" marker-end="url(#arr-sf)" />

  <rect class="node ok" x="240" y="196" width="200" height="70" rx="8" />
  <text class="t" x="340" y="224">STM32 hardware TRNG</text>
  <text class="s" x="340" y="242">analogue transistor noise</text>

  <line class="edge" x1="440" y1="231" x2="756" y2="241" marker-end="url(#arr-sf)" />

  <rect class="node ok" x="760" y="196" width="145" height="110" rx="8" />
  <text class="s" x="832" y="224">Backup password,</text>
  <text class="s" x="832" y="239">7z salt, HSM user</text>
  <text class="s" x="832" y="254">secrets, SD</text>
  <text class="s" x="832" y="269">overwrite blocks</text>

  <!-- the hotfix rebind, routed clear of the libngu box -->
  <path class="edge dashed" d="M 520 78 C 445 100, 402 138, 368 192" marker-end="url(#arr-sf)" />
  <text class="el" x="520" y="170">the hotfix rebinds this to the same hardware</text>

  <style>
    .lane {
      font: 600 10px var(--font-ui);
      letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    }
    .lane.bad-t { fill: var(--danger); }
    .lane.ok-t { fill: var(--safe); }
    .node {
      fill: var(--surface-2);
      stroke: var(--rule-2);
      stroke-width: 1.25;
    }
    .node.bad {
      fill: var(--danger-soft);
      stroke: var(--danger);
    }
    .node.ok {
      fill: var(--safe-soft);
      stroke: var(--safe);
    }
    .t {
      font: 600 12.5px var(--font-ui);
      fill: var(--ink);
      text-anchor: middle;
    }
    .t.mono { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11.5px; }
    .s {
      font: 10.5px var(--font-ui);
      fill: var(--ink-3);
      text-anchor: middle;
    }
    .edge {
      stroke: var(--ink-3);
      stroke-width: 1.5;
      fill: none;
    }
    .edge.dashed { stroke-dasharray: 5 4; }
    .el {
      font: 10px var(--font-mono);
      fill: var(--ink-3);
      text-anchor: middle;
      paint-order: stroke;
      stroke: var(--surface);
      stroke-width: 4px;
    }
    .ah { fill: var(--ink-3); }
  </style>
</Fig>
